 "notes": "Segment revenue includes intersegment revenue (as in the 10-K segment table); 'Other' = Other revenue (Sky Germany, Comcast Spectacor, Xumo, Corporate) + eliminations for revenue, and for Adjusted EBITDA = Media/Studios/Theme Parks headquarters & other + Corporate & other + eliminations + the adjustments excluded from consolidated Adjusted EBITDA (Versant separation costs: $483M in 2025, $7M in 2024). Total = consolidated Adjusted EBITDA (non-GAAP) per the 10-K reconciliations (2025/2024 from FY2025 10-K, 2023 from FY2024 10-K). All three years taken from the FY2025 10-K segment presentation (5 segments, adopted in 2024; 2023 recast). Small 1M rounding differences between the segment sum and the 10-K 'Total' line (e.g. 2024 Adj. EBITDA 40,321 vs 40,322) are absorbed in 'Other'. Versant (MS NOW, CNBC, USA Network, Golf Channel, E!, Syfy, Oxygen...) was spun off on 2 Jan 2026 (Nasdaq: VSNT) and is still included in Media for these years. On 16 Mar 2026 Comcast published a revised, pro forma (ex-Versant) trending schedule with a new segment composition for 2024-2025 (e.g. pro forma Media Adj. EBITDA 2025 = 164, total pro forma Adj. EBITDA 34,506); not used here because it is non-GAAP pro forma and covers only 2024-2025."
